{"event_id": "aee4eba9c189", "event_type": "system_response", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T18:24:47.171072+00:00", "data": {"text": "We've got a few security tools deployed to keep an eye on things around here. Let me give you a quick rundown. We've got OSSEC installed, which is a great tool for monitoring system calls and detecting potential security threats. We're also running Snort, an IDS (Intrusion Detection System) that can sniff traffic for suspicious patterns. And, of course, we've got a Mauth (Multi-Authoritative Host) set up for SSH login attempts to prevent brute-force attacks. We're also using Fail2Ban to automatically ban IP addresses that make too many login attempts in a row.\n\nOh, and I think we've also got some local iptables rules set up to control incoming traffic, but I haven't had a chance to dig into the details of those. (laughs) You know how it is, always a few things to keep track of!", "persona_used": "novice"}, "source": "harness"}
